TEST 38475 -- ATMF - recover from USB drive
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-21, tb470
DUT:    IE520 4-member VCStack, AMF node "IE520-stk" (AMF Member)
Master: AR4050S-5G "4050-5g"
Precondition (from the case): "DUT requires virtual-link for this test"

VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- steps 1-3 PASS, step 4 is REFUSED BY THE PLATFORM.
         This is a HARD BLOCKER, measured, not inferred. Nothing was wiped;
         the bench is intact.

=========================== THE BLOCKER ===================================

    IE520-stk# atmf cleanup
    % This command cannot be run when another stack member is present

**`atmf cleanup` is not available to a VCStack on this build.** It requires a
standalone unit. Since `atmf cleanup` is step 4 of this case AND step 4 of
38474, NEITHER case can be executed against the IE520 while it is stacked.

The only way to run them on IE520 hardware is to break the stack down to a
single member, which changes the DUT from "a VCStack" to "a standalone IE520"
and therefore tests something different from what the bench is set up for.
That is a decision for Terrence, not a workaround to apply silently.

=========================== WHAT DID PASS =================================

STEP 1 -- "The DUT should be a member of an AMF network"               PASS
  Mastership handed to the AR4050S; DUT reads Role: Member, 3 nodes
  (IE520-stk, 4050-5g, x230-10GP).

PRECONDITION -- "DUT requires virtual-link"                            PASS
  The L2 atmf-link on po1 was removed and replaced with a virtual link over
  the existing vlan10 transit (10.10.10.1 <-> 10.10.10.2):
      vlink1  1  10.10.10.1  2  10.10.10.2  Tunnel State: Complete
      show atmf links ->  vlink1  Uplink  Full  4050-5g  Forwarding
                          1.0.2   Downlink Full x230-10GP Forwarding

STEP 2 -- "Insert a USB drive into the DUT"                            PASS
  28.9 GB stick. **It must be in the member that is ACTIVE MASTER** -- see the
  finding below; this cost two physical moves to establish.
      Backup Media .......... USB (Total 29584.1MB, Free 29466.2MB)

STEP 3 -- "Save the configuration on the DUT, this should create a recovery
           file on the USB. Recover file should be present on the USB drive"  PASS
      copy running-config startup-config
        -> Building configuration... [OK]
        -> File synchronization with stack members 1, 2, 4 successfully completed
      dir usb: before save  ->  atmf_recovery_file      2176 B  02:14:14
      dir usb: after  save  ->  atmf_recovery_file      2480 B  02:17:50
                                atmf_recovery_file_hash   16 B  02:17:50
  The recovery file exists and the save demonstrably refreshed it (size and
  timestamp both moved). PASS.

STEP 4 -- "Enter the command atmf cleanup"                       BLOCKED (above)
STEP 5 -- "When the DUT reboots it should recover its configuration file
           from the USB drive"                                   NOT REACHED

=========================== FINDING: AMF media must be on the STACK MASTER ==

AMF only recognises backup media in the member that is Active Master. Measured
across three combinations -- this was not assumed:

| USB is in | Active Master | show atmf backup -> Backup Media |
| --- | --- | --- |
| member 1 | member 3 | NONE ("% No backup media found on this device") |
| member 3 | member 1 | NONE |
| member 3 | **member 3** | **USB (29584.1MB)** |

Practical consequence for anyone repeating this: the stick must sit in the
member that will be master **on both sides of the wipe**. After `atmf cleanup`
the config is erased, so stack priorities are erased too and the stack holds a
DEFAULT election -- all priorities 128, lowest MAC wins. On tb470 that is
**member 3** (84e3.2787.0740, vs .0780 / .09c0 / .0ac0). So member 3 is the
correct home for the stick, and member 3 was pinned master with
`stack 3 priority 1` for the pre-wipe steps.

=========================== PREP DONE, STILL VALID =========================

If the destack decision is taken, this is already staged:
  - current release copied to the USB: IE520-awplus_main-20260913-1734.rel
    (40052759 B, 02:21:28). The stick's other release, IE520-tb470.rel, is the
    **Aug 09** build -- older than the running Sep 13 one; do not rely on it.
  - the AMF master (AR4050S) holds NO IE520 release (only AR4050S-5.5.1-2.1.rel)
    and reports Backup Media: NONE. **The USB is the only possible recovery
    source** -- nothing else on this bench can hand the stack a release.

=========================== BENCH STATE AT EXIT ============================

Untouched by the refused command: stack Normal operation, all four Ready,
flash still holds IE520-awplus_main-20260913-1734.rel, AMF 3 nodes, DUT is
Member, secure mode Disabled.
Diverged from baseline and NOT yet reverted: `stack 3 priority 1`, and the
stack<->4050 AMF path is a virtual link rather than po1 atmf-link.

